  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145966",
      "title": "Using API Routes For Pre-Rendering Pages",
      "lectureOrder": 323,
      "videoOrder": 300,
      "sourceHash": "016c0a22b5a501a9e810166177ff2eb502635e984133c35792710f2750684652",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 5.14,
          "en": "Now let's make this a bit more complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.14,
          "end": 9.77,
          "en": "What if I don't just wanna have my load feedback button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.77,
          "end": 14.77,
          "en": "but I also want to have a let's say /feedback route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.81,
          "end": 19.49,
          "en": "so not /api/feedback but just /feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.49,
          "end": 23.75,
          "en": "Which should load a new HTML page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 23.75,
          "end": 26.43,
          "en": "So a page rendered in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.43,
          "end": 28.75,
          "en": "which also lists my feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.75,
          "end": 33.32,
          "en": "So now I wanna add a new normal page, not an API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 33.32,
          "end": 36.77,
          "en": "but I wanna add a new normal page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.77,
          "end": 38.47,
          "en": "That is still possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.47,
          "end": 41.97,
          "en": "We can still add a feedback JS file here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 45.36,
          "en": "in the pages folder, but outside of API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.36,
          "end": 49.3,
          "en": "or as you learned ,alternatively, add a feedback folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.3,
          "end": 51.64,
          "en": "with a index JS file in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.64,
          "end": 54.13,
          "en": "That's the equivalent to having a file named",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.13,
          "end": 56.35,
          "en": "feedback JS on the level above.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.35,
          "end": 58.8,
          "en": "And that's therefore what I'll go with here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 61.06,
          "en": "and then in this index JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.06,
          "end": 62.93,
          "en": "instead of that feedback folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.93,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "we can again create our regular component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "the feedback page component which we export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.22,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "and then here we can of course also render our list of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 78.69,
          "en": "feedbacks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "And we can now of course also just fetch our feedback data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "whenever that component is rendered, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "with help of useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 90.98,
          "en": "to implement client's site data fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.98,
          "end": 93.88,
          "en": "as you learned it in the data fetching section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.88,
          "end": 97.63,
          "en": "but maybe we also wanna pre-render this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.63,
          "end": 101.45,
          "en": "and prefetch the data for pre-rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.45,
          "end": 103.95,
          "en": "And that is something which we would do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.95,
          "end": 107.513,
          "en": "by exporting an async function called getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.21000000000001,
          "end": 112.27000000000001,
          "en": "That's what you also learned before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.27000000000001,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "We can still use these features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 117.97999999999999,
          "en": "even if we also use API routes in the project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.97999999999999,
          "end": 121.3,
          "en": "Of course, I would say because using API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.3,
          "end": 122.9,
          "en": "is an extra feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.9,
          "end": 126.23,
          "en": "it doesn't change the way next JS works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.23,
          "end": 130.221,
          "en": "So we can still add regular pages with features like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.221,
          "end": 133.57,
          "en": "getStaticProps to also have some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.57,
          "end": 136.85,
          "en": "server-side or node JS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.85,
          "end": 140.323,
          "en": "that is executed there when this page is pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 143.55,
          "en": "Now, the interesting thing is though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.55,
          "end": 148.55,
          "en": "what if we now here want to fetch our feedback data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.31,
          "end": 152.18,
          "en": "for pre-rendering this page?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.18,
          "end": 157.18,
          "en": "So here through props in this component I expect to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.3,
          "end": 161.68,
          "en": "my feedback items let's say and I wanna map them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.68,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "into list items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 167.64,
          "en": "where I then still output item.text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.64,
          "end": 172.64,
          "en": "and where I then still have my key set to item.id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.89,
          "end": 177.23,
          "en": "But now feedback items should be received through props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.23,
          "end": 178.733,
          "en": "with help of getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 179.72,
          "end": 181.563,
          "en": "How can we now make that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 184.84,
          "en": "Well, we did see similar examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.84,
          "end": 187.3,
          "en": "in the data fetching sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.3,
          "end": 191.37,
          "en": "There we for example, also talked to Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.37,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "and we then use the fetch API here, the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "here inside of getStaticProps to still send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "to an API and get data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 204.79,
          "en": "And that works as you saw there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 204.79,
          "end": 207.4,
          "en": "But, whilst this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.4,
          "end": 211.32999999999998,
          "en": "absolutely fine for external APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 211.32999999999998,
          "end": 215.07999999999998,
          "en": "like the Firebase API, you should not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.07999999999998,
          "end": 219.1,
          "en": "use fetch inside of getStaticProps or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.1,
          "end": 223.69,
          "en": "getServerSideProps to talk to your own API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.69,
          "end": 227.61,
          "en": "Instead since this is all part of one project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.61,
          "end": 231.39,
          "en": "and therefore ultimately all served by one server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 232.94,
          "en": "What you should do instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.94,
          "end": 237.13,
          "en": "is write any note JS logic that should execute here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.13,
          "end": 239.043,
          "en": "directly inside of getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.1,
          "end": 243.18,
          "en": "So if we have some logic in our API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 245.87,
          "en": "which also might need to be executed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.87,
          "end": 248.48,
          "en": "inside of a regular page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 248.48,
          "end": 252.443,
          "en": "then we should just make it available through an export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 252.443,
          "end": 257,
          "en": "so that we can run the code to find in the API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257,
          "end": 260.22,
          "en": "directly here inside of getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.22,
          "end": 261.83299999999997,
          "en": "or getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 262.81,
          "end": 265.03,
          "en": "So that means that here in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.14,
          "end": 269.84,
          "en": "this code for building the feedback path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.84,
          "end": 271.57,
          "en": "and extracting the feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.57,
          "end": 275.86,
          "en": "should be executed directly here in getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.86,
          "end": 280.22,
          "en": "We just don't wanna set some response status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 280.22,
          "end": 282.06,
          "en": "and return a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282.06,
          "end": 284.93,
          "en": "because that's not what getStaticProps is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.93,
          "end": 287.61,
          "en": "This is just about producing the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.61,
          "end": 289.313,
          "en": "for our page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.88,
          "end": 293.38,
          "en": "But since I already have extract feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.38,
          "end": 296.65,
          "en": "and filled feedback path in separate functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.65,
          "end": 300.41,
          "en": "we can just export these functions to make them available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.41,
          "end": 304.23,
          "en": "outside of this API feedback JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.23,
          "end": 308.22,
          "en": "export both functions and then in index JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.22,
          "end": 310.65,
          "en": "we can import these functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 310.65,
          "end": 315.65,
          "en": "We can import from going up one level diving into API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 316.17,
          "end": 319.57,
          "en": "diving into feedback and import from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 319.57,
          "end": 322.96,
          "en": "or we put those functions into a separate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 322.96,
          "end": 325.99,
          "en": "other folder and file, right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 325.99,
          "end": 330.64,
          "en": "We could add a helpers folder on the root project level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 330.64,
          "end": 333.8,
          "en": "and store our functions in some file in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.8,
          "end": 335.65999999999997,
          "en": "That would also be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 335.65999999999997,
          "end": 338.65,
          "en": "But here I'm importing from the API feedback file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 338.65,
          "end": 342.35,
          "en": "and I'll import the build feedback path function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 342.35,
          "end": 345.293,
          "en": "and the extract feedback function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 346.33,
          "end": 348,
          "en": "Now, the cool thing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348,
          "end": 351.75,
          "en": "that next JS will detect that what we're importing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 351.75,
          "end": 354.56,
          "en": "isn't the end code that will only use inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 354.56,
          "end": 355.40999999999997,
          "en": "of getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 356.35,
          "end": 360.08,
          "en": "and therefore that code will still not be included",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 360.08,
          "end": 362.15,
          "en": "in the client side bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 362.15,
          "end": 365.83,
          "en": "I talked about this in earlier sections already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 365.83,
          "end": 370.33,
          "en": "Code used in getStaticProps and dependencies used in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 370.33,
          "end": 373.57,
          "en": "so imports used in there will not end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 373.57,
          "end": 377.06,
          "en": "in the client side code bundle if we're not using that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 377.06,
          "end": 379.423,
          "en": "anywhere in our client side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 380.42,
          "end": 381.3,
          "en": "So therefore here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 381.3,
          "end": 385.72,
          "en": "We can now call build feedback path to construct our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.5,
          "end": 389.49,
          "en": "file path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 389.49,
          "end": 391.61,
          "en": "And then we can get access to our data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 391.61,
          "end": 395.04,
          "en": "by calling extract feedback and passing in the file path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 396.24,
          "end": 398.8,
          "en": "and then we just return our standard object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 398.8,
          "end": 402.24,
          "en": "with the props key as we always do it in getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 403.40999999999997,
          "end": 407.49,
          "en": "and we expose our feedback items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 407.49,
          "end": 408.94,
          "en": "because that's what I'm looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 408.94,
          "end": 412.64,
          "en": "All my props here, which is my data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 412.64,
          "end": 416.33,
          "en": "because to date I'm extracting is that extracted error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 416.33,
          "end": 417.653,
          "en": "from feedback json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 418.52,
          "end": 423.17,
          "en": "So now we have that code here inside of our regular page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 423.17,
          "end": 425.97,
          "en": "instead of using fetch and sending a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 425.97,
          "end": 428.03,
          "en": "to our own API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 428.03,
          "end": 431.15,
          "en": "because when working with your own API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 431.15,
          "end": 435.14,
          "en": "and when requiring them in your regular pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 435.14,
          "end": 438.59,
          "en": "you should not send the HTTP request to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 438.59,
          "end": 441.87,
          "en": "but instead leverage the fact that it's all running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 441.87,
          "end": 444.76,
          "en": "on the same computer on the same server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 444.76,
          "end": 448.82,
          "en": "and therefore just import it and directly run that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
